# Managed by Ansible (infra/ansible/roles/firewall). Do not edit by hand.
#
# Accept-all host firewall, on purpose:
#  * The perimeter firewall is the OCI security list (infra/terraform/network.tf):
#    only 22 and 6443 from admin_cidr, and 80/443 from the internet, reach this VM.
#  * Oracle's stock rules in this file REJECT most INPUT and all FORWARD traffic,
#    which breaks k3s pod networking.
#  * k3s (kube-proxy, flannel, network policy controller) creates and owns its own
#    chains at runtime. Never save the live ruleset into this file: debconf autosave
#    is off, and do not run `netfilter-persistent save`.
#  * This also drops Oracle's InstanceServices OUTPUT chain (root-only access to the
#    169.254.0.0/16 iSCSI/metadata endpoints). This is a single-admin VM with no
#    untrusted local users.
*filter
:INPUT ACCEPT [0:0]
:FORWARD ACCEPT [0:0]
:OUTPUT ACCEPT [0:0]
COMMIT
